# Responsiveness & Motion

## Responsiveness (non-negotiable)

- Mobile-first. Verify every component at ~375px, ~768px, and ~1280px before done.
- Prefer `clamp()` / flex / grid over fixed pixel widths.
- No horizontal scroll at any breakpoint unless explicitly intended (e.g. carousel).
- Touch targets ≥ 44px on mobile.

## Animation

- Use `motion` (framer-motion), `lenis` for smooth scroll, `react-intersection-observer` for scroll reveals.
- Shared animation variants live only in `src/lib/animations.js` — reuse them; do not hand-roll easing/duration per component.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` globally (hook or CSS). Never ship motion that ignores it.
- Entrance animations: 200–400ms. Do not animate form inputs or primary nav in ways that delay interaction.
- Scroll reveals via `react-intersection-observer`, trigger once per element (no re-animation on scroll up/down) unless asked otherwise.
